      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Dates: X月X号 and 星期几",
      "body": "Chinese dates go from big to small: first the month, then the day. Put a number before 月 for the month and a number before 号 for the day, so 5月8号 is May 8th. To ask the date, swap the numbers for 几: 几月几号？ The days of the week are 星期 plus a number: 星期一 is Monday, up to 星期六, Saturday. To ask which day it is, say 星期几？",
      "examples": [
